From: Luca Jones <ljones@t0.technology>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: core: add SanDisk SN64G to broken SD cache quirks

SanDisk SN64G microSD cards (MID 0x03, OID 0x5344, PNM "SN64G") do not
implement the SD 6.x cache feature reliably. Intermittently the
extension register write that sets the Flush Cache bit fails with
-EILSEQ, and when the write does land the card never clears the bit, so
mmc_poll_for_busy() times out:

  mmc0: error -84 writing Cache Flush bit
  mmc0: Card stuck being busy! __mmc_poll_for_busy

Either way the flush request is reported as failed to the block layer,
which makes ext4 abort its journal and remount read-only:

  I/O error, dev mmcblk0, sector 124454236 op 0x1:(WRITE) flags 0x9800
  Aborting journal on device mmcblk0p3-8.
  EXT4-fs error (device mmcblk0p3): ext4_journal_check_start:84: \
      Detected aborted journal
  EXT4-fs (mmcblk0p3): Remounting filesystem read-only

Data CRC errors accumulate in mmc err_stats while Command CRC errors and
Tuning errors stay at zero, and the flash itself passes a full badblocks
run -- the failure is confined to the cache flush command, not the bus
and not the media.

This is the same failure mode as the existing Kingston Canvas Go! Plus
entry, so reuse MMC_QUIRK_BROKEN_SD_CACHE. Observed on cards from
11/2025, but no date restriction is applied since the defect is tied to
the card model.

Signed-off-by: Luca Jones <ljones@t0.technology>
---
 drivers/mmc/core/quirks.h | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/quirks.h b/drivers/mmc/core/quirks.h
index 92905fc46436..3ea3ee2ba1ba 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/quirks.h
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/quirks.h
@@ -21,6 +21,16 @@ static const struct mmc_fixup __maybe_unused mmc_sd_fixups[] = {
 	 * This has so far only been observed on cards from 11/2019, while new
 	 * cards from 2023/05 do not exhibit this behavior.
 	 */
 	_FIXUP_EXT("SD64G", CID_MANFID_KINGSTON_SD, 0x5449, 2019, 11,
 		   0, -1ull, SDIO_ANY_ID, SDIO_ANY_ID, add_quirk_sd,
 		   MMC_QUIRK_BROKEN_SD_CACHE, EXT_CSD_REV_ANY),

+	/*
+	 * SanDisk SN64G microSD cards intermittently fail the extension
+	 * register write that sets the SD cache Flush Cache bit with
+	 * -EILSEQ, and when the write does land the card never clears the
+	 * bit, so mmc_poll_for_busy() times out. Either way the flush
+	 * request fails and ext4 aborts its journal.
+	 */
+	MMC_FIXUP("SN64G", CID_MANFID_SANDISK_SD, 0x5344, add_quirk_sd,
+		  MMC_QUIRK_BROKEN_SD_CACHE),
+
 	END_FIXUP
 };

